<div class="figure-title">One plan; fresh runs can still diverge</div>
<div class="figure-intro">Markdown inline parsing · A recorded rewrite case from the preceding RSR paper</div>
<div class="connection" data-from="source-generate" data-to="source-prebuilt" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:374px;top:206px;width:64px;transform:rotate(0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="source-prebuilt" data-to="source-pass" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:764px;top:206px;width:64px;transform:rotate(0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="source-pass" data-to="shared-plan" data-relation="extract"><div class="edge " style="left:990px;top:284px;width:36px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div><div class="edge " style="left:990px;top:320px;width:390px;transform:rotate(180deg)"></div><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:600px;top:320px;width:42px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="shared-plan" data-to="a-parser" data-relation="independent-reexecution"><div class="edge " style="left:600px;top:504px;width:38px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div><div class="edge " style="left:600px;top:542px;width:292px;transform:rotate(180deg)"></div><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:308px;top:542px;width:80px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="shared-plan" data-to="b-inspect" data-relation="independent-reexecution"><div class="edge " style="left:600px;top:504px;width:38px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div><div class="edge " style="left:600px;top:542px;width:292px;transform:rotate(0deg)"></div><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:892px;top:542px;width:80px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="a-parser" data-to="a-feedback" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:308px;top:764px;width:62px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="b-inspect" data-to="b-feedback" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:892px;top:764px;width:62px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="a-feedback" data-to="a-pass" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge feedback arrow" style="left:308px;top:968px;width:62px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="b-feedback" data-to="b-fail" data-relation="sequence"><div class="edge failure arrow" style="left:892px;top:968px;width:62px;transform:rotate(90deg)"></div></div><div id="source-generate" class="node " style="left:48px;top:128px;width:326px;height:156px"><div class="label">Source · Turn 26</div><div class="name">Try parser generation</div><div class="sub">Prepare a text parser</div><span hidden data-node-detail>The successful source trajectory tries tree-sitter generate at turn 26. tree-sitter is a toolkit for generating and using parsers, which turn Markdown text into structures a program can process. The diagram shows key events selected in the paper.</span></div><div id="source-prebuilt" class="node " style="left:438px;top:128px;width:326px;height:156px"><div class="label">Source · Turn 51</div><div class="name">Use a prebuilt parser</div><div class="sub">Load a compiled component</div><span hidden data-node-detail>A prebuilt parser is an already compiled parsing component that can be loaded directly in a compatible environment. The source trajectory uses it at turn 51. The paper abbreviates the command as tree-sitter parse -l ...node --lang-name markdown /tmp/test.md.</span></div><div id="source-pass" class="node result" style="left:828px;top:128px;width:324px;height:156px"><div class="label">Source · Final check</div><div class="name">64 turns, passed</div><div class="sub">Success informs the plan</div><span hidden data-node-detail>The source run takes 64 turns and passes final verification. Its successful experience is distilled into a plan that guides the model through the task again in a fresh environment.</span></div><div id="shared-plan" class="node runbook" style="left:180px;top:362px;width:840px;height:142px"><div class="label">The same runbook, distilled from success</div><div class="plan"><span>Compatible parser</span><span class="sep">→</span><span>Match output summaries</span><span class="sep">→</span><span>Table-handling options</span></div><span hidden data-node-detail>A runbook records key procedures, checks, and recovery steps. This plan distills the successful source run into finding a compatible parser, matching output summaries, and checking table-handling options. A and B below execute independently in separate fresh environments.</span></div><div id="a-parser" class="node " style="left:48px;top:622px;width:520px;height:142px"><div class="label">Rerun A · Turn 9</div><div class="name">Use a prebuilt parser</div><div class="sub">Reach a working parser early</div><span hidden data-node-detail>Rerun A uses a prebuilt parser at turn 9. It shares the plan with B on the right, but each runs in its own fresh environment. The source excerpt at turn 51 records this operation too.</span></div><div id="b-inspect" class="node failed" style="left:632px;top:622px;width:520px;height:142px"><div class="label">Rerun B · Turn 26</div><div class="name">Inspect parse output</div><div class="sub">Terminal: inspection tool not found</div><span hidden data-node-detail>Rerun B tries xxd .../parse.txt | head -20; the terminal returns bash: xxd: command not found. xxd is a command-line tool for viewing or converting hexadecimal file contents. This event records a failed tool call.</span></div><div id="a-feedback" class="node " style="left:48px;top:826px;width:520px;height:142px"><div class="label">Rerun A · Turn 21</div><div class="name">Check rebuilt output</div><div class="sub">Run the feedback script</div><span hidden data-node-detail>Turn 21 checks the rebuilt output with python3 /app/tools/feedback; feedback is the result-checking script used here.</span></div><div id="b-feedback" class="node " style="left:632px;top:826px;width:520px;height:142px"><div class="label">Rerun B · Turn 36</div><div class="name">Recheck after edits</div><div class="sub">Run feedback again</div><span hidden data-node-detail>After making changes, rerun B runs the feedback result-checking script again at turn 36. This and turn 26 are two execution events selected in the paper.</span></div><div id="a-pass" class="node result" style="left:48px;top:1030px;width:520px;height:104px"><div class="label">Rerun A · Final check</div><div class="name">32 turns, passed</div><span hidden data-node-detail>Rerun A takes 32 turns and passes final verification. The successful trajectory then undergoes quality and leakage screening before it can become a training demonstration.</span></div><div id="b-fail" class="node failed" style="left:632px;top:1030px;width:520px;height:104px"><div class="label">Rerun B · Final check</div><div class="name">38 turns, failed</div><span hidden data-node-detail>Rerun B takes 38 turns and fails final verification. It is filtered out at the final check; the excerpts show its tool-inspection and result-checking steps.</span></div>
