          "html": "<div class="canvas"><div class="label heading" style="left:42px;top:27px;">TB-GAE: terminal feedback across turns</div><div class="label " style="left:42px;top:83px;width:1110px;">Let γ = 0.9, λ = 0.8, q = γλ = 0.72; only the terminal reward is 1.</div><div class="label row" style="left:42px;top:186px;">Interaction</div><div class="label " style="left:318px;top:128px;">Turn 1</div><div class="label " style="left:836px;top:128px;">Turn 2</div><div class="node token" id="G-input1" data-map-node style="left:300px;top:171px;width:70px;height:76px"><div class="action">g₁</div><div data-node-detail>The 1st illustrative generated position in the turn-1 command. Real commands usually contain more tokens.</div></div><div class="node token" id="G-input2" data-map-node style="left:425px;top:171px;width:70px;height:76px"><div class="action">g₂</div><div data-node-detail>The last illustrative generated position in the turn-1 command. After the tool call finishes, the environment returns observations.</div></div><div class="node observation" id="G-input-observation" data-map-node style="left:550px;top:171px;width:210px;height:76px"><div class="action">o₁ … o<sub>L</sub></div><div data-node-detail>The environment returns L observation tokens. They remain in the next turn’s model context; only the advantage recursion below skips these positions. The comparison uses L=3 for readability.</div></div><div class="node token" id="G-input3" data-map-node style="left:815px;top:171px;width:70px;height:76px"><div class="action">g₃</div><div data-node-detail>The first generated position of turn 2. The policy and Critic inputs still include the previous turn’s tool output.</div></div><div class="node token" id="G-input4" data-map-node style="left:940px;top:171px;width:70px;height:76px"><div class="action">g₄</div><div data-node-detail>The last generated position of turn 2. The example truly terminates the task here and applies the terminal reward once.</div></div><div class="node reward" id="G-inputR" data-map-node style="left:1070px;top:171px;width:90px;height:76px"><div class="action">R = 1</div><div data-node-detail>Set terminal reward R=1. At true termination, the successor value and recursive advantage term are 0.</div></div><div class="connection" data-from="G-input1" data-to="G-input2" data-relation="main"><div class="edge main arrow" style="left:370px;top:209px;width:55.0px;transform:rotate(0.0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="G-input2" data-to="G-input-observation" data-relation="main"><div class="edge main arrow" style="left:495px;top:209px;width:55.0px;transform:rotate(0.0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="G-input-observation" data-to="G-input3" data-relation="main"><div class="edge main arrow" style="left:760px;top:209px;width:55.0px;transform:rotate(0.0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="G-input3" data-to="G-input4" data-relation="main"><div class="edge main arrow" style="left:885px;top:209px;width:55.0px;transform:rotate(0.0deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="G-input4" data-to="G-inputR" data-relation="main"><div class="edge main arrow" style="left:1010px;top:209px;width:60.0px;transform:rotate(0.0deg)"></div></div><div class="label " style="left:300px;top:267px;width:840px;">Observations stay in context; only GAE recursion skips them.</div><div class="rule" style="left:42px;top:321px;width:1118px"></div><div class="label section" style="left:42px;top:342px;">One run, three clocks for credit assignment</div><div class="label row" style="left:42px;top:419px;width:220px;">All-token chain<span>Both token types</span></div><div class="node token " id="GA-g1" data-map-node style="left:300px;top:416px;width:70px;height:72px"><div class="action">g₁</div><div data-node-detail>Generated position g1. In the mixed-text chain, both generated and observed positions enter the advantage recursion. Even when observation positions are masked in the training loss, they 