          "html": "<div class="canvas"><h2 class="case-title">Rust–C: two recorded runs</h2><div class="case-subtitle">One task, two independent evaluations: execution first, final verification next.</div><div class="task"><span>Task</span>Deliver an auto-building calculator whose output exactly matches the hidden reference.</div><h3 class="lane-heading" style="top:278px">Base<small>Independent run A · Local success, final failure</small></h3><div class="edge-label" style="left:789px;top:487px">Final checks</div><div class="divider" style="top:1017px"></div><h3 class="lane-heading" style="top:1064px">RPR-2<small>Independent run B · Terminal-RSI-27B</small></h3><div class="edge-label" style="left:789px;top:1720px">Final checks</div><section id="base-arithmetic" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Test nesting and large integers" style="left:160px;top:344px;width:510px;height:190px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Test nesting and large integers"><span class="index">E60 · Local tests</span><h3>Test nesting and large integers</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Observed</span>Local arithmetic passes</div><div class="node-line"><span class="key">State</span>Computes; final checks pending</div><div data-node-detail>Base event E60 tests nested expressions and large integers; one addition returns 1000000001. After local arithmetic passes, final verification still checks exact output on hidden inputs.</div></section><section id="base-build" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Clean build outputs; run entry" style="left:160px;top:570px;width:510px;height:185px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Clean build outputs; run entry"><span class="index">E62 · Clean rebuild</span><h3>Clean build outputs; run entry</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Observed</span>Automatic compilation succeeds</div><div class="node-line"><span class="key">State</span>Local wrapper check passes</div><div data-node-detail>Base event E62 deletes build outputs to test whether the entry point can compile automatically. This local wrapper check succeeds, showing that the build path works.</div></section><section id="base-wrapper" class="node success" data-map-node data-map-label="Auto-build passes" style="left:800px;top:542px;width:340px;height:159px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Auto-build passes"><span class="index">Check 1 · Wrapper</span><h3>Auto-build passes</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Result</span>Entry point works</div><div data-node-detail>The final verifier’s wrapper gate passes. Build verification and output-equivalence verification are separate checks.</div></section><section id="base-fuzz" class="node failure" data-map-node data-map-label="Exact match fails" style="left:800px;top:790px;width:340px;height:195px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Exact match fails"><span class="index">Check 2 · Hidden inputs</span><h3>Exact match fails</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Actual</span><code>23</code></div><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Reference</span><code>23.0</code></div><div data-node-detail>Figure 16 explicitly shows division with an integer-valued result returning 23, versus the reference output 23.0. Numerically similar values still violate the exact-string output contract, so the hidden fuzz equivalence check fails.</div></section><div class="note" style="left:160px;top:806px;width:510px">It runs and passes local arithmetic.<br>Output formatting still causes final failure.</div><div class="milestone" data-node="base-arithmetic" style="left:103.5px;top:402.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:409px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="milestone" data-node="base-build" style="left:103.5px;top:628.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:635px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="connection" data-from="base-arithmetic" data-to="base-build" data-relation="main"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:110px;top:416px;width:212.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="base-build" data-to="base-wrapper" data-relation="verification"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:670px;top:621px;width:130.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="base-wrapper" data-to="base-fuzz" data-relation="verification"><div class="edge failure arrow" style="left:970px;top:701px;width:89.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><section id="rpr-tools" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Find audio tools" style="left:160px;top:1132px;width:510px;height:157px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Find audio tools"><span class="index">E1–2 · Find tools</span><h3>Find audio tools</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">State</span>Prepare to read task information</div><div data-node-detail>In the first RPR-2 run, events E1–2 discover audio-processing tools. This diagram follows the events selected in the paper.</div></section><section id="rpr-toolchain" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Check the toolchain" style="left:160px;top:1333px;width:510px;height:157px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Check the toolchain"><span class="index">E10 · Inspect environment</span><h3>Check the toolchain</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">State</span>Then build the new implementation</div><div data-node-detail>E10 checks the toolchain. This event, the new implementation files in E11, and the local build check in E16 belong to the same RPR-2 run.</div></section><section id="rpr-build" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Create C / Rust components" style="left:160px;top:1534px;width:510px;height:187px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Create C / Rust components"><span class="index">E11 · Write files</span><h3>Create C / Rust components</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Code</span>C code with a Rust interface</div><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Entry</span>Compile an executable</div><div data-node-detail>E11 writes a C AST (an abstract syntax tree organizing expressions into operators and operands), recursive evaluation and deallocation functions, and Rust foreign-function declarations (the interface for calling C). The C archive uses -fPIC (position-independent code), and the entry script requests a musl target (a C standard-library implementation). Subsequent expression evaluation is performed through Python calls.</div></section><section id="rpr-probes" class="node " data-map-node data-map-label="Check linking; evaluate with Python" style="left:160px;top:1776px;width:510px;height:224px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Check linking; evaluate with Python"><span class="index">E11–16 · Check and run</span><h3>Check linking; evaluate with Python</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Observed</span>Local tests return 14, 256</div><div class="node-line"><span class="key">State</span>Return Python output unchanged</div><div data-node-detail>The first RPR-2 run performs a C-linking smoke test (a quick check that cross-language components connect and run), then calls Python from the Rust entry point to evaluate expressions and print the output unchanged. E16 shows static-pie linking (a relocatable, statically linked executable); expression evaluation depends on the Python runtime.</div></section><section id="rpr-wrapper" class="node success" data-map-node data-map-label="Auto-build passes" style="left:800px;top:1776px;width:340px;height:159px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Auto-build passes"><span class="index">Check 1 · Wrapper</span><h3>Auto-build passes</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Result</span>Entry point works</div><div data-node-detail>The protected RPR-2 wrapper check passes. Both RPR-2 evaluations independently pass this check.</div></section><section id="rpr-fuzz" class="node success" data-map-node data-map-label="Equivalence passes" style="left:800px;top:2024px;width:340px;height:159px" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Equivalence passes"><span class="index">Check 2 · Hidden inputs</span><h3>Equivalence passes</h3><div class="node-line"><span class="key">Result</span>Hidden ref. matched</div><div data-node-detail>This RPR-2 run passes the fuzz equivalence check on hidden inputs. Both independent RPR-2 evaluations pass auto-build and output-equivalence checks; the diagram shows selected events from the first run.</div></section><div class="milestone" data-node="rpr-tools" style="left:103.5px;top:1190.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:1197px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="milestone" data-node="rpr-toolchain" style="left:103.5px;top:1391.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:1398px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="milestone" data-node="rpr-build" style="left:103.5px;top:1592.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:1599px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="milestone" data-node="rpr-probes" style="left:103.5px;top:1834.5px"></div><div class="edge  " style="left:117px;top:1841px;width:43.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div><div class="connection" data-from="rpr-tools" data-to="rpr-toolchain" data-relation="main"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:110px;top:1204px;width:187.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="rpr-toolchain" data-to="rpr-build" data-relation="main"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:110px;top:1405px;width:187.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="rpr-build" data-to="rpr-probes" data-relation="main"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:110px;top:1606px;width:228.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="rpr-probes" data-to="rpr-wrapper" data-relation="verification"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:670px;top:1855px;width:130.00px;transform:rotate(0.00deg)"></div></div><div class="connection" data-from="rpr-wrapper" data-to="rpr-fuzz" data-relation="verification"><div class="edge  arrow" style="left:970px;top:1935px;width:89.00px;transform:rotate(90.00deg)"></div></div><div class="note" style="left:160px;top:2054px;width:520px">Both checks pass.<br>This run still depends on Python.</div><div class="divider" style="top:2230px"></div><div class="footer" style="top:2260px">E denotes event IDs selected in the paper. Base and RPR-2 are independent runs.<br>Source: Terminal-RSI, Appendix H / Figure 16. Green: check passed; orange: failed.</div></div>"
